    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "When you were a child, did you also have trouble staying organized or remembering everyday tasks?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, yeah, definitely. Even back in elementary school... I was always that kid who forgot permission slips, or I'd somehow lose my finished homework right in my own backpack. I had this huge purple backpack, I think it was from L.L. Bean? You know how those things last forever? My mom actually still uses it to store her knitting supplies. She knits these amazing little baby blankets, she just made a really cute yellow one for my cousin's new baby. \n\nBut yeah, my backpack was just a total black hole for papers. And school projects were the worst. I always needed my mom or my teacher to literally sit there and remind me, like, step by step to actually finish them. Otherwise I'd just get caught up in picking out the right markers for the cover page and completely forget to do the actual work.",
