      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Um, no, I wouldn't say *significant* problems. Like, my husband gets a little annoyed sometimes when I forget to do things around the house, but it's not a huge deal. Like last week, I left the wet clothes in the washing machine for two days and they got that awful mildew smell. You know how hard it is to get that out of towels? I had to buy this special vinegar wash stuff online. The bottle took forever to ship, too, because I think it came all the way from Oregon. \n\nI've always wanted to visit Oregon, actually. My sister went to Portland a few years ago and said the food trucks there are just incredible. She had this gourmet grilled cheese with, like, fig jam and brie on sourdough. I actually tried to recreate it at home once, but I totally burned the bread because I walked away to answer a work email and completely forgot the pan was on the stove. The smoke alarm went off and everything. We had to open all the windows and order pizza instead. We usually get from Luigi's down the street, they have the absolute best garlic knots. They put this little side of marinara in the box that is just perfectly seasoned. \n\nBut, um... wait, what was I saying? Oh, right, relationships and work. Yeah, no, my husband just kind of sighed and ate the pizza. We don't really have big fights about my forgetfulness or anything. And at work, like I said, I'm still getting by without any real trouble. So no, nothing major.",
